## The five tabs

- **Observations** — what staff recorded about your child, usually with photos.
- **Student** — your child's profile, with **Details**, **Attendance** and **Reports** tabs.
- **Calendar** — what's coming up.
- **Themes** — the theme plans the setting is working through.
- **Payments** — your payment records.

The bell icon at the top of each screen opens **Announcements** from the school. A red badge counts
the ones you haven't opened yet (it shows **9+** past nine).

{% callout type="note" %}
Staff call observations **activities** in their own app. If a teacher refers to "the activity I
added", that's the same thing you see under **Observations**.
{% /callout %}

## Finding a particular observation

Observations filter by **growth milestone**, **activity type** and **date**, with **Clear** to reset
them. The list loads more as you scroll to the bottom. The growth-milestone filter is the useful one when you want to see progress in a single area
over time rather than reading the feed day by day.

## Your child's profile

The **Student** tab is the same profile page the teacher sees, with three tabs:

- **Details** — your child's information, with allergies and medicine highlighted.
- **Attendance** — a calendar by month showing days present, working days and an attendance
  percentage.
- **Reports** — the written reports your child's teacher has **published**. Drafts are never shown.

You can update your **mobile number**, **email** and **address**, and change your child's **photo**
(use the pencil, then **Save Changes**). Everything else is fixed by the school; ask the teacher or
office if it is wrong.

## Payments

The Payments tab lists your payment records and takes you out to the payment page when something is
due. If it says no payment records were found, the setting hasn't raised anything against your
account — it isn't a sign the app failed to load them.

## More than one child, or more than one parent

**One login can hold several children at the same school.** Tap your child's initial or photo at the
top of the screen to see the children on the account, tap one to **switch child**, or choose
**Manage children & accounts**. You'll find the same screen under **Account → Switch child**.

On the **Switch child** screen:

- **Children on this account** lists each child with their class; the one you are viewing is
  ticked. Switching reloads every tab for that child, so nothing from the previous child lingers.
- **Add another child** asks for the child's **Student ID**, then **Send code**: a code goes to the
  phone number or email the school has on file for that child. Enter it and tap **Add child**. Only
  children at the *same school* as this account can be added.
- With more than one child, the **⋮** menu offers **Remove from account**. A child shown as "No
  longer on the school's records" can't be switched to.

A child at a **different school** needs a separate parent account. Those appear under **Other parent
accounts**; **Sign in to a different parent account** adds one. Switching to another account signs
you out of the current one, and accounts are saved **on the device**:

- A new phone starts with no saved accounts. That's expected — sign in once and it's saved again.
- The ✕ beside a saved account takes it off *that device only*. The account itself still exists,
  and you can sign back in with it.

## Logging out and deleting your account

**Account → Log out** signs you out. Under **Danger zone**, **Delete account** permanently removes
your login and signs you out; it asks you to confirm and can't be undone.

